================================================================================
NAME ATTRIBUTION
================================================================================

The name "Spinning Arrow" is taken from:

    Röttger, Hofmann, Pyatkin, Hinck, Kirk, Schütze, and Hovy.
    "Political Compass or Spinning Arrow? Towards More Meaningful Evaluations for
    Values and Opinions in Large Language Models." ACL 2024.
    https://arxiv.org/abs/2402.16786

That paper's finding — that forced-choice value scores shift with framing, lack
paraphrase robustness, and diverge from open-ended answers — is the reason this project
reports fragility as a first-class metric. The authors are not affiliated with this
project and have not endorsed it.
